 value of the county&rsquo;s 6 grids runs 75 years back to 1951, and October to November came in under 90% of normal in 36 of them, more than any other pair. In 2025 that same pair ran 47% of normal, and November to December ran 34%. So far in 2026, March to April came in at 26% of normal on the middle of the grids. Every grid had its driest year in 2007, with grid 17899 at 67% that year.</p>"}
